<http://data.silknow.org/object/33b11384-b742-30a9-9f47-33279e643021/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Panel depicting Kannon a Bodhisattva of Mercy (Japanese version of the Chinese Kuan-yin) embroidered on the background woven with an all-over pattern of dragons on a blue ground. The border, also on a blue ground, is woven with a scrolling lotus and chrysanthemum design.\n\nShe is shown standing on a Lotus throne. In the left hand the divinity holds a lotus flower and the right hand is in the An-i-in (Vitarka) mudra- symbol of discussion.\n \nThe image was made in various techniques.\n\nEmbroidery of the Bodhisattva is in laid and couched gold thread, silk cord and floss silks. \n\nHalo: silk cord and radiating aura in silver thread, 2 threads together couched. \n\nBackground: tissue (lampas) with dark blue ground, woven in tabby and two pattern wefts, buff and pale blue, also woven in tabby one shoot ground weft; one shoot pattern weft: one shoot pattern weft. Repeat: L. 2.625 ins, W. 2.25 ins.\n\nBorder: dark blue satin ground, woven with a pattern in gilt-paper strip, bound only by the decoupures. Repeat: L.6 ins, W over 4 ins- incomplete."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/33b11384-b742-30a9-9f47-33279e643021> .

